P('yonder','From Old English geond, “beyond or over there”; it is an old-fashioned or literary word for a place some distance away.',[
 C('yonder.s1','文学','The guide pointed across the stream and said the old mill stood over yonder.','向导指向溪流对岸，说老磨坊就在那边。','over yonder; go yonder','Adverb: at or toward a place some distance away.','The mill is across the stream.'),
 C('yonder.s2','文学','A narrow path led to the yonder hill, where the shepherd kept a small stone shelter.','一条窄路通往远处那座山丘，牧羊人在那里有一间小石屋。','the yonder hill / field','Adjective: situated at some distance away.','Yonder modifies the distant hill.')],[M('The guide pointed at the ground under his feet and called it yonder, although the word refers to a distant place.','The guide pointed across the stream and called the distant mill yonder.','Yonder means over there at a distance, not immediately beneath the speaker.')],[
 Q('yonder.q1','yonder.s1','context','Where did the guide say the old mill stood?','Across the stream, some distance away.','Directly beneath his feet.','Inside his backpack.','Over yonder refers to a distant place.'),
 Q('yonder.q2','yonder.s2','meaning','What did yonder describe before hill?','A hill some distance away.','A hill beneath the speaker.','A hill made of wool.','As an adjective, yonder means situated at a distance.'),
 Q('yonder.q3','yonder.s1','register','What style does yonder often have?','Old-fashioned or literary.','A modern technical measurement.','A formal plural pronoun.','Yonder is an archaic or literary directional word.'),
 Q('yonder.q4','yonder.s1','distinction','Which expression means “over there at a distance”?','over yonder','under my wrist','inside the writ','Over yonder points to a distant place.')]);
