P('your','From Old English eower, the possessive form of you; it can refer to an addressee, people generally, or a typical example in informal speech.',[
 C('your.s1','语法','Please write your name on the visitor badge before entering the workshop.','进入车间前，请把你的名字写在访客证上。','your name / book / coat','Possessive determiner: belonging to the person or people addressed.','The badge should bear the addressee’s name.'),
 C('your.s2','通用','In a crowded train, your personal space can disappear quickly.','在拥挤的列车上，人们的个人空间可能很快消失。','your typical / ordinary person','Generic possessive determiner referring to people in general.','Your means one’s in a general statement.'),
 C('your.s3','口语','He arrived with your classic oversized hat and a story about missing the last bus.','他戴着那种典型的夸张大帽子来了，还讲了个错过末班车的故事。','your classic / usual + noun','Informal use meaning the typical or familiar kind.','The phrase identifies a recognizable type.')],[M('Please write your name on my visitor badge, although the badge belongs only to me and not to you.','Please write your name on your visitor badge.','Your marks something belonging to the addressee, not solely to the speaker.')],[
 Q('your.q1','your.s1','context','Whose name should go on the visitor badge?','The person entering the workshop.','The workshop’s owner only.','The name of a yew tree.','Your refers to the addressee’s name.'),
 Q('your.q2','your.s2','meaning','What does your mean in “your personal space can disappear”?','People’s personal space in general.','Only one named person’s coat.','The train’s destination.','This is generic your, meaning one’s or people’s.'),
 Q('your.q3','your.s3','register','What does “your classic oversized hat” mean?','A familiar or typical kind of oversized hat.','A hat legally owned by the listener.','A hat from a distant past that is unavailable.','Informal your classic describes a recognizable type.'),
 Q('your.q4','your.s1','grammar','What kind of word is your in “your name”?','A possessive determiner before a noun.','A noun replacing the whole phrase.','A past-tense verb.','Your modifies the noun name to show possession.')]);
P('yours','Possessive pronoun from your + the independent possessive -s pattern; it stands for something belonging to the addressee and appears in letter closings.',[
 C('yours.s1','语法','My umbrella is black, but the red one by the door is yours.','我的伞是黑色的，但门边那把红伞是你的。','This / that one is yours.','Possessive pronoun: belonging to the person or people addressed.','Yours replaces “your umbrella.”'),
 C('yours.s2','书面','Yours sincerely, Helen Park','谨启，海伦·帕克','Yours sincerely / faithfully','Traditional complimentary close in a formal letter.','Yours is part of the letter closing.')],[M('The red umbrella is yours, so it belongs to me and not to you.','The red umbrella is mine, so it belongs to me and not to you.','Yours indicates possession by the addressee, while mine indicates the speaker.')],[
 Q('yours.q1','yours.s1','meaning','Which umbrella belongs to the person being addressed?','The red one by the door.','The speaker’s black one.','Both belong to a stranger.','Yours replaces the phrase “your umbrella.”'),
 Q('yours.q2','yours.s2','context','Where might “Yours sincerely” appear?','At the end of a formal letter.','On a yardstick.','In a recipe for yoghurt.','It is a conventional complimentary close.'),
 Q('yours.q3','yours.s1','grammar','Why can yours stand alone?','It is a possessive pronoun replacing a noun phrase.','It must always directly precede a noun.','It is a plural form of you are.','Yours can replace “your + noun.”'),
 Q('yours.q4','yours.s2','distinction','Which phrase is a letter closing?','Yours faithfully','Your umbrella','You are faithful','Yours faithfully is a conventional closing expression.')]);
P('yourself','A compound of your + self; it is the singular reflexive or emphatic form of you and can mean alone or without help.',[
 C('yourself.s1','语法','You should remind yourself to lock the workshop door before leaving.','离开前你应该提醒自己锁好车间的门。','remind / teach / introduce yourself','Reflexive pronoun referring back to the singular subject you.','The person reminds the same person who acts.'),
 C('yourself.s2','语法','You yourself noticed that the wristwatch stopped whenever the room grew cold.','你本人也注意到了，只要房间变冷，腕表就会停。','you yourself','Emphatic pronoun emphasizing the person addressed.','Yourself adds emphasis to you.'),
 C('yourself.s3','通用','You can assemble the shelf yourself if you follow the instructions one step at a time.','只要按步骤阅读说明，你可以自己组装这架搁板。','do something yourself; by yourself','Pronoun meaning alone or without another person’s help.','The addressee can do the task independently.')],[M('You should remind yourself to lock the door, meaning you should remind another person instead of yourself.','You should remind yourself to lock the door.','A reflexive pronoun refers back to the subject you.')],[
 Q('yourself.q1','yourself.s1','grammar','Who should the addressee remind to lock the door?','The same person being addressed.','A group of strangers.','The workshop door itself.','Yourself refers back to the subject you.'),
 Q('yourself.q2','yourself.s2','meaning','What does “you yourself noticed” emphasize?','The addressee personally noticed it.','The speaker’s wristwatch noticed it.','No one noticed it.','Yourself is emphatic in this sentence.'),
 Q('yourself.q3','yourself.s3','context','How can the shelf be assembled?','Alone, without help, by following instructions.','Only by hiring a whole crew.','Without using any instructions or tools.','Yourself can mean without another person’s help.'),
 Q('yourself.q4','yourself.s1','distinction','Which sentence uses yourself reflexively?','You cut yourself while carving the wood.','You yourself chose the design.','You assembled it yourself.','In the first, yourself receives the action done by you.')]);
P('yourselves','A compound of your + selves, the plural reflexive or emphatic form of you used when addressing more than one person.',[
 C('yourselves.s1','语法','Please make yourselves comfortable while the guide checks the museum tickets.','导游核对博物馆门票时，请各位随意坐好。','help / introduce / prepare yourselves','Plural reflexive pronoun referring back to you when addressing multiple people.','The instruction is addressed to the whole group.')],[M('The guide told the visitors to make yourselves comfortable, but spoke to one person using singular you.','The guide told the visitors to make themselves comfortable.','When referring to visitors as third person, use themselves; yourselves directly addresses a group.')],[
 Q('yourselves.q1','yourselves.s1','meaning','Who should make themselves comfortable?','The group of visitors being addressed.','One visitor’s coat.','The guide’s employer.','Yourselves is plural and addresses more than one person.'),
 Q('yourselves.q2','yourselves.s1','context','What was the guide checking?','The museum tickets.','The visitors’ yardsticks.','A ship’s wool sail.','The sentence says the guide checks the tickets.'),
 Q('yourselves.q3','yourselves.s1','grammar','Which sentence correctly addresses several people?','Please introduce yourselves to the group.','Please introduce yourself to the group, everyone.','Please introduce youselves to the group.','Yourselves is the standard plural reflexive form.'),
 Q('yourselves.q4','yourselves.s1','distinction','When is yourselves appropriate?','When speaking directly to multiple people.','When speaking to one person about a third person.','When naming a group of yew trees.','Yourselves is the plural form used for direct address.')]);
